========================================================================================================
S01 -- THE RUNNING-a0 SYNTHESIS:  Phi(x) = (g_obs^2 - g_bar^2)/(a0 g_bar)
        a0 = 9.36190e-11 m/s^2 (committed footing);  x-window log10 x in [-1.5, +0.3]
========================================================================================================
PRE-REGISTERED VERDICT RULE (fixed before any Phi statistics):
  COLLAPSE of a universal running-a0 law Phi(x)  <=>  BOTH
    C1: in >= 2/3 of overlapping bin-survey comparisons,
        |Phi_survey - Phi_SPARC_bin| < 3 * sqrt(SE_s^2 + SE_bin^2)  AND
    C2: shared power-law exponent p (fit a, SPARC+dwarfs): |p|/SE_p > 5.
  Comparison inventory (geometry-fixed): every in-window survey point whose x
  lies in a SPARC bin with >= 5 rings from >= 2 galaxies.
  Expected overlaps per the brief: SPARC-vs-O01 around x~0.08-0.11,
  SPARC-vs-MW around x~0.26-0.32 (outermost two annuli) and x~0.4-1.24,
  SPARC-vs-MIGHTEE at x~0.034 (deep-cut median).
========================================================================================================

